## 3.0.24 (2026-11-23)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Fix settings reverting or disappearing after updates and restarts by unifying Rust and frontend access onto a single `tauri-plugin-store` instance instead of two competing stores.
-   Keep built-in `openai_ocr` recognition services in `recognize_service_list` on startup instead of stripping them during service validation.
-   Serialize and flush pending frontend config writes before closing windows or switching settings pages, and remove a redundant `store.load()` race on mount.

## 3.0.23 (2026-11-23)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Fix `ReferenceError: config is not defined` when opening the Translate settings page caused by an unquoted overlay theme i18n key.

### Improvements:

-   Build and publish only the Windows x64 installer and updater bundle in the Windows release workflow.

## 3.0.22 (2026-11-23)

### New features:

-   Overlay translation: automatically scale each block's font size to match the original OCR text size instead of capping at the default app font size, while keeping multi-line paragraphs proportional.
-   Overlay translation: add adaptive light/dark theme from sampled screen background colors, vertical text orientation support, and batch translation for LLM/batch-friendly services.

### Improvements:

-   Use single-pass in-memory WinRT OCR for overlay recognition and reclaim border/padding space inside tight OCR text boxes for better readability.
-   Add a unified centered loading indicator and expand overlay layout/OCR unit test coverage.

### Bugs fixed:

-   Fix Windows mouse hook lag/races, WebView2 reselect deadlock, font shrink-back on manual scaling, and overlay resize/drag geometry sync.

## 3.0.21 (2026-11-22)

### New features:

-   Overlay translation: copy the translation, the original text, or both, and switch between original and translated text.
-   Overlay translation: pin the overlay so outside clicks no longer close it; a pin badge marks the locked pinned state.
-   Overlay translation: show failures in an inline status bar with retry failed blocks, switch channel, copy error, retry OCR, reselect, and open settings.
-   Overlay translation: remember the font size, and keep the channel chosen with "switch channel" for later retries and overlays.

### Improvements:

-   Place the overlay toolbar above or below the selection instead of over the first translated line; use an inset toolbar only when the selection fills the screen.
-   Reload overlay service, model, and OCR settings before refresh or retry, and keep the overlay pinned while the settings window is open.
-   Ignore outside clicks while the overlay is hidden for a refresh, and recover from failed show calls.
-   Make the overlay status bar scrollable on narrow selections, keep the toolbar close button reachable, and let the OCR error card pass clicks through to the toolbar.

## 3.0.20 (2026-11-20)

### New features:

-   Add show/hide buttons for API keys in service configuration, including plugin fields.

### Bugs fixed:

-   Remember the settings window size and position across restarts, including the first open after launch.

## 3.0.19 (2026-11-20)

### New features:

-   Add an OpenAI-compatible recognition service with address presets, model fetching and a disable-thinking option.

### Improvements:

-   List the OpenAI-compatible service first when adding a translation or recognition service.

## 3.0.18 (2026-11-19)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Open the settings window on Tauri's main thread, so opening it from the HTTP API no longer deadlocks.
-   Rework the settings layout to right-aligned controls; proxy, hotkey, backup and plugin fields are no longer clipped or wrapped.
-   Default the settings window to 760x560, keep it from being resized narrower than 760, and remember its size and position.
-   Read saved configuration before the first render, prefetch the autostart state and render font dropdowns before the font list arrives, so switching pages no longer shifts the layout.
-   Start every settings page at the top instead of keeping the previous page's scroll offset.

## 3.0.17 (2026-11-19)

### New features:

-   Add a "Disable thinking" option to OpenAI-compatible translation providers.

### Bugs fixed:

-   Align the network proxy host/port and username/password fields.
-   Unify the widths of overlay translation controls and place hints under their fields.
-   Let hotkey inputs fill the available row instead of leaving the right side empty.
-   Load saved configuration before writing defaults, and remember the settings window size and position.
-   Show full-width inputs in plugin/service configuration dialogs and enlarge the dialog.

## 3.0.16 (2026-11-19)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Remove the white square corners outside the rounded configuration window on Windows.

## 3.0.15 (2026-11-18)

### Notes:

-   Start a new updater signing key. Existing installations must install 3.0.15 manually once before automatic updates resume.

## 3.0.14 (2026-11-18)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Close Windows overlay translation only when clicking outside the overlay, instead of when the window loses focus.
-   Show translating and failed states in the overlay, time out unresponsive translation channels, and report the channel, error details and troubleshooting steps.
-   Do not cache empty translation results, so refreshing the overlay requests them again.

## 3.0.13 (2026-11-18)

### New features:

-   Allow choosing the OCR engine used by Windows overlay translation.
-   Keep the overlay window at the selected region size and fit translated text within each OCR box.
-   Use a single selection-sized translation block when the chosen OCR engine does not return text boxes.

## 3.0.12 (2026-11-18)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Fix the translate window rendering an empty transparent frame because `TargetArea` crashed on an undefined `useAtom`.
-   Show a readable message instead of a blank window when a window fails to render.
-   Keep loading the remaining plugins when one plugin fails to load.

## 3.0.11 (2026-11-18)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Point the About page GitHub, issue and discussion links at this repository.

## 3.0.10 (2026-11-18)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Show the translate window from the backend so a missed frontend event can no longer leave it hidden.
-   Keep the translate window inside the current monitor when the saved position is off-screen.
-   Keep the screenshot overlay open on an accidental click instead of closing it as a too-small selection.

## 3.0.9 (2026-11-17)

### Bugs fixed:

-   Register every global shortcut even when one is already taken by another application.
-   Skip clipboard monitoring for empty or overly long text.
-   Skip the translate window when there is no text to translate.

## 3.0.8 (2026-11-17)

### New features:

-   Add Windows overlay translation with OCR-backed text replacement.
-   Add OpenAI-compatible endpoint presets and model selection for overlay translation.

### Bugs fixed:

-   Improve screenshot translation capture and window activation.
-   Prevent long overlay translations and adjacent text boxes from being clipped.
-   Improve configuration window resizing, shortcut field sizing, and control borders.
-   Because this release starts a new updater signing key, existing installations must install 3.0.8 manually once before automatic updates resume.

